msgid "help.config_b1"
msgstr "1. Protection engine: select the protection level (Full, Technical & network, or Personal data & GDPR), protected copy suffix, and file input method."

msgid "help.config_b2"
msgstr "2. Window & system: configure what happens when clicking close [X] or minimize [-], the startup tab, and visible navigation tabs."

msgid "help.config_b3"
msgstr "3. Clipboard & alerts: adjust notification style when intercepting text, timed auto-wipe, and the bottom CLI dock."

msgid "help.config_b4"
msgstr "4. Appearance, language & security: choose language, visual theme, accent color, font size, button style, and vault inactivity auto-lock."

msgid "help.config_h4"
msgstr "Configuration & ergonomics"

msgid "help.config_p1"
msgstr "The Settings tab is organized into 4 functional blocks with a top action bar to save, reset, or inspect logs at any time:"

msgid "help.config_persist_note"
msgstr "All settings are persisted in ~/.lexishield/config.toml."

msgid "help.logs_h4"
msgstr "Diagnostics & telemetry logs"

msgid "help.logs_p1"
msgstr "The log console records every event from the native Rust engine (Tauri calls, vault reads/writes, detections, and transformations). You can enable debug mode for verbose traces or filter by level (INFO, WARN, ERROR)."

msgid "help.pairs_h4"
msgstr "Token pairs management (1:1 bijectivity)"

msgid "help.pairs_op1"
msgstr "Add pair: lets you preload custom associations (e.g. your name with a protected value of your choice)."

msgid "help.pairs_op2"
msgstr "Quick search & clear: filter by original or protected value and click ✕ to clear the search box instantly."

msgid "help.pairs_op3"
msgstr "Omit token: if a keyword or technical term should never be replaced, select it and click Omit."

msgid "help.pairs_op4"
msgstr "Backups (.bak): automatic backups created when modifying pairs can be restored individually from the Vaults table."

msgid "help.pairs_ops_title"
msgstr "Main operations:"

msgid "help.pairs_p1"
msgstr "Whenever LexiShield detects or replaces a sensitive token, it creates a bijective mapping in the active vault. This guarantees that the same confidential entity always receives the exact same protected value across all your documents."

msgid "help.pwd_h4"
msgstr "Why does LexiShield require a password for its vaults?"

msgid "help.pwd_p1"
msgstr "LexiShield was engineered to protect enterprise-grade secrets and highly confidential personal data. A password is mandatory for three non-negotiable architectural reasons:"

msgid "help.pwd_principle"
msgstr "Fundamental principle: Zero-Knowledge architecture"

msgid "help.pwd_r1"
msgstr "Immunity to physical or forensic attacks: if someone accesses your hard drive, without the master password it is mathematically impossible to reconstruct the link between protected values and real secrets."

msgid "help.pwd_r2"
msgstr "Argon2id + ChaCha20-Poly1305 cryptography: the decryption key is never stored in any file; it is derived via memory-hard Argon2id parameters to neutralize GPU and ASIC brute-force attacks."

msgid "help.pwd_r3"
msgstr "Strict per-project or per-client isolation: by assigning different passwords to different vaults (.lexi), you guarantee an impenetrable cryptographic wall for each client or environment."

